Command summary: items in [] are optional
                 items in <> are mandatory, but the shown item is
                       just an example
                 items separated by a | mean you must pick one of them

  cd <dirname>
     --- changes the current directory to "dirname"
  dir [time] [file] [dirs] [size] [new]
     --- lists the files and directories in the current directory,
         various options control what is listed
         time  -- shows times/dates on files
         file  -- only show files
         dirs  -- only show subdirectories
         size  -- show sizes of files
         new   -- show files sorted by date, most recent first
  top
     --- takes you to the top of the directory tree
  xdown <filename>   (or use get or dl)
     --- use selected protocol to download a file called "filename"
  xup <filename>     (or use put or ul)
     --- use selected protocol to upload a file called "filename"
  describe <filename>
     --- show the long file description about a file
  alias perm|temp <mycom> <some vbbs command string>
     --- allows you (or the Sysop) to build custom commands, or make
         abbreviated commands.  The "perm" and "temp" flags indicate
         whether this is a permanent alias or it is a temporary one
         that will be discarded at the next menu change.
  display <filename>
     --- used by the Sysop in menu files to display text menus (like this
         one).  To see this file type: "display help"
  prompt <filename>
     --- used by the Sysop in menu files to set the small prompting
         menu.
  confer
     --- type this command to join the multi-user conference, to exit from
         the conference type a CTRL-Z character.
  bye
     --- type this command to exit from the BBS.
  login
     --- type this command to log into your account to set your
         access level.  Normally you will not have to do this, as it
         is done in the first screen.
  feedback next|prev|first|last|again|goto|enter|reply [number]
     --- this command is used to read the feedback message section, usually
         the Sysop will alias it (like I have done in the message section)
         next  = show next message         prev = show previous message
         first = show first message        last = show last message
         again = show message again        goto = goto message number
         enter = enter a new message      reply = reply to the current msg
         "number" is an optional number used in the "goto" command.
  password
     --- use this command to change your password
  upgrade
     --- use this command to upgrade your account by caching in
         an IceBBS access coupon for this BBS.
